Source: ps3-games
Section: games
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Tiberiu Chibici <chibicitiberiu@gmail.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.7.2
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: ps3-games
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ps3-games-integration (= ${binary:Version}), ${games:Depends}
Description: the PS3's game suite
 The games this distribution is tested and benchmarked with: each one known to run on the RSX, with
 its sound, joins this package once it does (gamedb build.toml suite = "free" or "licensed"). Remove
 this package to remove them. Only free packages: the licensed game data is in ps3-games-licensed.

Package: ps3-games-free
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ps3-games-integration (= ${binary:Version}), ${games:Depends}
Suggests: ${games:Suggests}
Description: the PS3's game suite (free data only)
 Games from the PS3 game suite that do not require non-redistributable or proprietary game data to
 run (gamedb build.toml suite = "free"). Games whose data is licensed are suggested only: this public
 metapackage variant leaves them out.

Package: ps3-games-integration
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Breaks: ps3-desktop (<< 0.893)
Replaces: ps3-desktop (<< 0.893)
Description: Walnut's menu entries and settings for the PS3's games
 The games' integration into the PS3 desktop, from the games database (gamedb desktop/): menu
 entries that start each game's modes through ps3-game (game mode), shown only when the game is
 installed; the PS3 defaults some games read from system-wide files (e.g. OpenArena's); the games'
 own menu entries that ours stand for, diverted out of the menu; the list of old per-user files
 ps3-migrate-home tidies up.
